{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtopreviewandtest"]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" calls into a real "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":". For previews and tests, swap it for "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — an actor that records every call and exposes its history for assertions. The mock has no Mixpanel dependency and runs offline."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"In a SwiftUI preview","anchor":"In-a-SwiftUI-preview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Inject a mock-backed store and the analytics work flows without spinning up the SDK:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["#Preview {","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: MockMixpanelAnalyticsService())","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This requires that ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppStore.configured","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accepts an injected ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". See Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" guide for the factory pattern.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"In a Swift Testing suite","anchor":"In-a-Swift-Testing-suite"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the mock to verify mapper behavior. Await the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to make assertions deterministic:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","import Testing","","@Test","func incrementMapsToCounterAdded() async {","    let mock = MockMixpanelAnalyticsService()","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: mock)","","    store.send(.counter(.increment(5)))","    await store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","","    let events = await mock.trackedEvents","    #expect(events.first?.name == \"counter_added\")","    #expect(events.first?.properties[\"amount\"] == .int(5))","}"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Asserting on identify and alias","anchor":"Asserting-on-identify-and-alias"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mock records identify and alias calls in order:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Test","func userSignInIdentifies() async {","    let mock = MockMixpanelAnalyticsService()","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: mock)","","    store.send(.auth(.signIn(userID: \"user-1\")))","    await store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","","    let calls = await mock.identifyCalls","    #expect(calls == [.init(userID: \"user-1\", properties: [\"tier\": .string(\"free\")])])","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" is an actor, so its accessors are async — wrap them in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Drive ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites without touching Mixpanel’s network.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"How to Preview and Test","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"iden